{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he sent his brothers.</b> Meaning, all of them, and Binyamin with them. And so it says in Yosef's words (Genesis 45:9): ״מַהֲרוּ וַעֲלוּ אֶל אָבִי וְגוֹ׳ וְהִנֵּה עֵינֵיכֶם וְגוֹ׳ וְעֵינֵי אָחִי בִנְיָמִין״ — see how he validates the matter in Ya'akov's heart through the testimony of Binyamin who sees. And from this point on, one can no longer maintain the explanation that Yehudah's bones were rolling about because he failed to fulfill his word; rather, it was because a ban imposed conditionally requires release, as they of blessed memory stated (Makkot 11:)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The Or HaChaim here alludes to the midrashic tradition that Yehudah's bones rolled in his coffin until Yosef released the ban; the verse וַיְשַׁלַּח is read as implying a formal release (התרת נידוי)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:00.430521327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}